WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.082 --> 00:00:03.141
(ripping effect)

00:00:03.141 --> 00:00:04.293
- Lorraine says hi.

00:00:04.293 --> 00:00:07.994
And Lorraine from South
Carolina: "I'm stuck.

00:00:07.994 --> 00:00:09.925
"I'm hoping that you
can help me get unstuck.

00:00:09.925 --> 00:00:12.529
"My career, my living
arrangements all need an overhaul,

00:00:12.529 --> 00:00:14.642
"I'm so overwhelmed right now.

00:00:14.642 --> 00:00:16.162
"How do I start?

00:00:16.162 --> 00:00:17.477
"Thank you," Lorraine.

00:00:17.477 --> 00:00:21.163
- Hey Lorraine. I think
when you feel overwhelmed,

00:00:21.163 --> 00:00:22.493
you feel stuck.

00:00:22.493 --> 00:00:24.733
I think you kind of of,
in this moment Lorraine,

00:00:24.733 --> 00:00:26.472
it's really probably a call

00:00:26.472 --> 00:00:29.374
just to create a bit
of a reflective space.

00:00:29.374 --> 00:00:33.531
And come back to think
of, what is your big idea

00:00:33.531 --> 00:00:34.767
going to solve?

00:00:34.767 --> 00:00:36.941
And who is the audience?

00:00:36.941 --> 00:00:38.664
And what is their pain point?

00:00:38.664 --> 00:00:41.035
And how can you help them
overcome that pain point?

00:00:41.035 --> 00:00:43.891
And a beauty about this,
particularly when you become

00:00:43.891 --> 00:00:46.761
overwhelmed and you've got
to-do list kind of this long,

00:00:46.761 --> 00:00:50.844
is cut back to the essence of your idea,

00:00:50.844 --> 00:00:52.443
your product, your service.

00:00:52.443 --> 00:00:54.110
And why it's going to change the world?

00:00:54.110 --> 00:00:55.397
And then the other thing,

00:00:55.397 --> 00:00:57.451
you know, the magic of simplification.

00:00:57.451 --> 00:01:00.439
You know, what does it
do that you can actually,

00:01:00.439 --> 00:01:04.080
in a consumer product, make
the consumer's life better?

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:06.323
Or a B-2-B sort of world,

00:01:06.323 --> 00:01:08.525
really try to take hostile,

00:01:08.525 --> 00:01:10.113
or improve their top line,

00:01:10.113 --> 00:01:12.714
or take hassle out of their organization

00:01:12.714 --> 00:01:14.613
and less stress.

00:01:14.613 --> 00:01:16.884
So I think you just got
to come back to basics.

00:01:16.884 --> 00:01:19.417
Just focus on where's your audience,

00:01:19.417 --> 00:01:22.998
what idea is going to kind
of really change the world

00:01:22.998 --> 00:01:26.226
and create a market for
your product or service.

00:01:26.226 --> 00:01:27.928
And then if you do that,

00:01:27.928 --> 00:01:30.908
you can get really clear
about what's important.

00:01:30.908 --> 00:01:33.231
And actually one other thing.

00:01:33.231 --> 00:01:36.531
I hope I'm kind of not doing
motherhood and apple pie here.

00:01:36.531 --> 00:01:39.425
But loads of people get into

00:01:39.425 --> 00:01:41.552
you know, this is urgent, this
is urgent, this is urgent,

00:01:41.552 --> 00:01:43.350
and their, kind of, to-do
list grows and grows

00:01:43.350 --> 00:01:44.852
and becomes overwhelming

00:01:44.852 --> 00:01:46.539
and your head's spinning.

00:01:46.539 --> 00:01:50.001
I'd ask yourself if you got a mission,

00:01:50.001 --> 00:01:51.792
what's really important?

00:01:51.792 --> 00:01:55.850
'Cause everything, everything
could appear urgent,

00:01:55.850 --> 00:01:58.496
but there's very few things
that are really important.

00:01:58.496 --> 00:02:01.301
And what's going to really move the dial?

00:02:01.301 --> 00:02:04.606
And then just focus your
urges about moving the dial

00:02:04.606 --> 00:02:06.590
and actually Lorraine,
what you can do mentally

00:02:06.590 --> 00:02:08.377
is create a bucket in the corner,

00:02:08.377 --> 00:02:10.530
and if there's lots of good ideas,

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:12.750
and they're not fundamentally important,

00:02:12.750 --> 00:02:14.887
just right 'em down,
chuck it in the bucket.

00:02:14.887 --> 00:02:16.944
Come back to 'em in 90 day's time.

00:02:16.944 --> 00:02:19.027
But really focus on what's important.

00:02:19.027 --> 00:02:22.802
And, you know, I'd say where
you get confidence from

00:02:22.802 --> 00:02:25.419
is not only the idea
and then the strategy,

00:02:25.419 --> 00:02:29.424
but where you get success
from is awesome execution.

00:02:29.424 --> 00:02:31.442
Really executing the hell out of an idea.

00:02:31.442 --> 00:02:32.842
- I agree with you.

00:02:32.842 --> 00:02:34.509
I echo a lot of what you said.

00:02:34.509 --> 00:02:36.206
I think you've got to just simplify.

00:02:36.206 --> 00:02:38.487
I would look at what is the one thing

00:02:38.487 --> 00:02:40.740
that if I focused on,

00:02:40.740 --> 00:02:42.435
that would really have a big impact

00:02:42.435 --> 00:02:43.753
and have a ripple effect.

00:02:43.753 --> 00:02:46.249
'Cause once you start making
progress on one thing,

00:02:46.249 --> 00:02:47.538
and you're getting getting some results,

00:02:47.538 --> 00:02:50.270
it bleeds into everything
else you're doing.

00:02:50.270 --> 00:02:52.235
Once you're confident,
you're more confident

00:02:52.235 --> 00:02:54.255
in a business deal,

00:02:54.255 --> 00:02:57.571
you become more confident in
your personal life, as well.

00:02:57.571 --> 00:02:58.404
It bleeds through everything.

00:02:58.404 --> 00:03:00.484
And so I'd be looking at,

00:03:00.484 --> 00:03:02.213
okay, there's a thousand
things that you have to do,

00:03:02.213 --> 00:03:04.026
what's the one single most important thing

00:03:04.026 --> 00:03:06.407
that if you fix this,

00:03:06.407 --> 00:03:08.628
it will not only help
that once situation but

00:03:08.628 --> 00:03:10.025
everything around it as well.

00:03:10.025 --> 00:03:12.165
And then focus on doing that

00:03:12.165 --> 00:03:14.622
and eliminate the distractions around it.

00:03:14.622 --> 00:03:17.180
(ripping sound effect)

